% ======================================================================================== 4 Methodology
\section{Methodology}\label{sec:method}
\para{Fast tier and v2} A detector fires on a \(\geq\)<< V('pol.det_c') >>¢ move of the 10\,s VWAP against the prior
60\,s. Each month a wallet qualifies on past months only (\(\geq\)<< V('pol.q_prints') >> prints 0--3\,s after a
detection, \(\geq\)<< V('pol.q_matches') >> matches, \(t > << V('pol.q_t') >>\) on its 30\,s markout). The frozen book
v2 copies qualifying prints, sized \(\propto 1/\sqrt{q(1-q)}\), at most << V('risk.order_usd') >> per order and
<< V('risk.netcap') >> shares net per match, held to resolution, at the fast tier's own prices: \emph{the opportunity at
their speed, not our execution}.

\para{CV strategy} Streamed causally on held-out 120\,fps table-tennis video, our live engine calls
<< V('cv.eng.tp') >> of << V('cv.eng.nmiss') >> misses before contact, none wrongly (Wilson lower bound
<< V('cv.eng.wil_lo') >>; median lead << V('cv.eng.lead') >>\,ms);
an offline evaluation with a look-ahead feature called << V('cv.tt.tp50') >> of << V('cv.tt.called50') >> at 50\,ms (Fig.~\ref{fig:ladder}b). Frame to order-ready over
WebRTC takes << V('e2e.ours') >>\,ms; with a simulated 1\,s feed, network and venue hold, << V('e2e.total') >>\,ms, under
the organiser's 3\,s bar (\texttt{results/e2e}, paper). With the bounce at time zero an order wins only if
\begin{equation}\label{eq:budget}
  V + \delta + D - \ell \;<\; L + R \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad V \;<\; L + R - D - \delta + \ell ,
\end{equation}
where \(V\) is the feed delay, \(\delta\) the inference (<< V('cv.inf') >>\,ms), network and gateway, \(D\) the
<< V('venue.delay') >>\,s taker delay, \(\ell\) the call lead, \(L\) the stamp lag and \(R\) the reprice relative to the
stamp, measured on << V('lat.n_points') >> live points (fills draw on the << V('cv.pool.d3') >> whose book moved
\(\geq\)3¢); \(V\) runs 0--60\,s, << V('cv.seeds') >> seeds a cell. The trade set is every historical point the market
later repriced \(\geq\)<< V('pol.det_c') >>¢: \emph{selected on outcomes, not ex ante}. \(L\) is unmeasured:
pre-registered << V('cv.pre.lag') >>\,s, or a post hoc estimate of << V('cv.cal.lag') >>\,s (95\% CI
<< V('cv.cal.lag_ci') >>\,s; two modes, as the stamp has 1\,s resolution) that assumes the first informed prints are
courtside humans reacting in << V('cv.cal.react') >>\,s (who would also queue ahead of a 1\,s-feed order). Free of \(L\), the call must land
\(\geq\)<< V('cv.call_before_stamp') >>\,s before the umpire's stamp; \(V = 1\)\,s at \(L = << V('cv.cal.lag') >>\)\,s
equals a camera << V('cv.cal.shift') >>\,s \emph{ahead} of the bounce at \(L = << V('cv.pre.lag') >>\)\,s. Its
pre-registration set no pass/fail rule; the blind test of the frozen v3 rule did, and failed (Table~\ref{tab:fail}).

\para{Costs} Each match's own taker fee,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:fee}
  f(q) = r\,q\,(1-q)\ \text{per share} \;=\; 10{,}000\,r\,(1-q)\ \text{bps of notional},
\end{equation}
with \(r = << V('fee.rate') >>\) today (<< V('fee.bps_q05') >>\,bps at \(q = 0.5\)): << V('v2.is.fee_bps') >>\,/\,<< V('v2.oos.fee_bps') >>\,bps
on v2's trades (IS\,/\,OOS). Spreads are paid as traded. Stresses: ½ and 1 tick worse entry, fees \(\times\)2,
all costs \(\times\)2 (\(\approx\)+<< V('v2.is.hs_bps') >>\,bps more). \para{Validation} Walk-forward inside IS; the fee in force;
the onset look-ahead fixed (D9); every read of held-out data logged.

