% ======================================================================================== 5 Results
\section{Results}\label{sec:results}
The fast tier beats other takers every month and copying it 3\,s later loses (Fig.~\ref{fig:edge}a). At its fills v2
earns in both periods (Table~\ref{tab:v2}, Fig.~\ref{fig:edge}b); out of sample the edge is gone at ½ tick
worse entry (<< V('v2.oos.slip05') >>¢) and negative with fees doubled (<< V('v2.oos.fx2.c') >>¢,
<< V('v2.oos.fx2.mpos') >> months positive).
\para{Sharpe above 3} We assumed a bug and found one: fixing the onset look-ahead (D9) cut IS Sharpe from
<< V('v2.onset.is.sr') >> to << V('v2.is.sr') >>. The rest is about << V('v2.trades_per_day') >> small, nearly
independent bets a day (same-day correlation << V('risk.corr_sameday') >>). The deflated Sharpe \citep{bailey2014} is
<< V('rig.dsr.is') >> IS at \(N = << V('rig.N3386') >>\) but << V('rig.dsr.oos') >> OOS: 40 days cannot rule out luck.
The CV Sharpe is a seed mean over trades selected on outcomes.
\para{The 1\,s baseline} At the pre-registered lag the CV trader makes << V('cv.pre.is.usd') >>\,/\,<< V('cv.pre.oos.usd') >>
a day (IS\,/\,OOS; Sharpe << V('cv.pre.is.sr') >>\,/\,<< V('cv.pre.oos.sr') >>); at the post hoc estimate
<< V('cv.cal.is.usd') >>\,/\,<< V('cv.cal.oos.usd') >> (Sharpe << V('cv.cal.is.sr') >>\,/\,<< V('cv.cal.oos.sr') >>;
Table~\ref{tab:cv}, Fig.~\ref{fig:decay}). That figure is fragile: at its interval's low end it is about
<< V('cv.at_lo.is.usd') >>\,/\,<< V('cv.at_lo.oos.usd') >>, and the same inference read per point falls to
<< V('cv.stc.oos.usd') >> (break-even << V('cv.stc.be.is') >>\,/\,<< V('cv.stc.be.oos') >>\,s). The live engine's own
calls barely move the cells. Two biases flatter the sweep: trades chosen on outcomes, and a reprice timed
<< V('rp.recv_ms') >>\,ms late. The tests free of them lose: a replay of << V('rp.matches') >> matches
recorded live on 2026-10-03 on their real books loses in << V('rp.cells_neg') >> of << V('rp.cells') >> settings
(<< V('rp.v1l2.c') >>¢ at \(V = 1\)\,s; Fig.~\ref{fig:replay}), and an ex-ante Markov-swing filter (exploratory) in
<< V('rp.sel.neg2') >> cells (Table~\ref{tab:A-sel}), so the feed delay, not the selection, sinks the 1\,s trader; the
frozen v3 rule failed blind (Table~\ref{tab:fail}).

