% ======================================================================================== 6 Risk
\section{Risk management}\label{sec:risk}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Limits, in code} (\texttt{engine/risk/}). << V('risk.order_usd') >> per order, << V('risk.netcap') >>
shares net per match, zone << V('risk.zone') >>: one match can lose at most << V('risk.maxloss') >> plus fees. Capital
3\(\times\) peak locked (v2 << V('v2.is.cap') >>; CV << V('cv.pre.oos.cap') >>--<< V('cv.cal.is.cap') >>). Kill
switches: stale feed \(>\)<< V('risk.feed_stale') >>\,s, vision \(>\)<< V('risk.vision_stale') >>\,s, latency above its
rolling p95, manual; the << V('risk.daily_stop') >> daily stop (<< V('risk.daily_stop_sigma') >>\,\(\sigma\) of v2's
daily P\&L) is a disaster stop.
\item \textbf{CV model risk.} Wrong calls always fill (Table~\ref{tab:cv}). MISS calls trade only at confidence
\(\geq\)0.95 and positive edge after the fee (code); live use needs 73 audited correct calls in a row, and a confirmed
false call halts the day (policy). Phantom calls outside play (about << V('cv.phantom.hr') >> an hour) erase the
1\,s OOS P\&L at << V('cv.phantom.pre') >> (pre-registered) or << V('cv.phantom.cal') >> (post hoc) a day, so the
rally-state gate (coded, off, unevaluated) must be on. Betting video at 25--50\,fps without early calls gives
<< V('cv.pess.is.usd') >>\,/\,<< V('cv.pess.oos.usd') >> a day (pre-registered).
\item \textbf{De-risking, set in advance} (policy, not code; it never fired in sample, so it is untested on a decline).
Halve size if the trailing 30-day edge is below << V('pol.trail_half') >>¢ (IS minimum << V('risk.trail_min') >>¢);
stop at \(\leq 0\), a << V('pol.dd_stop') >> drawdown, or a fee or delay change. At the fast tier's decay, v2's OOS
<< V('v2.oos.c') >>¢ halves size in << V('risk.months_half') >> months and stops in << V('risk.months_zero') >>. The CV
book starts only on a measured \(L \geq << V('cv.L_go') >>\)\,s.
\item \textbf{Tail, venue, legal.} Fees \(\times\)2 erase v2's OOS edge; kurtosis
<< V('v2.is.kurt') >>\,/\,<< V('v2.oos.kurt') >>. The UMA oracle settles (disputes: 4--6 days); collateral is pUSD,
so only working capital sits on the venue \citep{pmuma}; US persons are close-only \citep{pmgeoblock}; courtsiding
breaches ticket terms \citep{itf2026}. Factors \citep{fama1993,carhart1997}: \(\alpha\) \(t = << V('fac.alpha_t') >>\),
max \(|t| = << V('fac.max_t') >>\), R² << V('fac.r2') >> (IS; Table~\ref{tab:A-factor}).
\end{itemize}

% ======================================================================================== 7 Liquidity
\section{Liquidity and capacity}\label{sec:liq}
v2 trades << V('v2.is.notional_day') >> a day, << V('v2.is.share_vol') >> of match volume; its OOS CI excludes zero
only up to 1\(\times\) size (<< V('cap.1x.oos.capital') >>) and 5\(\times\) loses (Fig.~\ref{fig:cap}a). Median stale
depth before a reprice: << V('liq.stale_pre') >>\,/\,<< V('liq.stale_1s') >>\,/\,<< V('liq.stale_2s') >> at
0\,/\,1\,/\,2\,s; spread << V('liq.spread') >>¢. The CV book (Table~\ref{tab:cv}: 10 matches a day, half the stale
depth) at the post hoc estimate halves its Sharpe at << V('capcv.half.oos') >> of capital OOS
(<< V('capcv.half.oos.day') >>/day) and << V('capcv.half.is') >> IS (<< V('capcv.half.is.day') >>/day), or
<< V('capcv.halfall.oos') >>\,/\,<< V('capcv.halfall.is') >> covering every match; at the pre-registered lag its Sharpe
is << V('capcv.pre.sr0.is') >>\,/\,<< V('capcv.pre.sr0.oos') >> at the smallest size: no capacity. Its notional is
<< V('capcv.share_inplay') >> of in-play volume but << V('capcv.share_fast') >> of the fast tier's 0--3\,s volume: the
seconds after each point bind. Fixed costs decide: the book can pay at most << V('cv.cal.oos.maxlic') >> a month for
data OOS (post hoc) or << V('cv.pre.oos.maxlic') >> (pre-registered), against an assumed licence of
<< V('fin.feed.low') >>--<< V('fin.feed.high') >>; the central << V('fin.fixed.central') >>-a-day stack is covered at no
\(L \leq << V('cv.L_central') >>\)\,s, the cheapest (<< V('fin.fixed.low') >>) only at \(L \geq\) << V('cv.L_go.range') >>\,s.
Covering every match, the camera-free stack (<< V('capcv.cf.is.cost') >>--<< V('capcv.cf.oos.cost') >> a day) breaks
even from about << V('capcv.cf.is') >> (IS) and << V('capcv.cf.oos') >> (OOS) of capital (\texttt{results/capacity}); v2's
OOS break-even fee is << V('fin.be_fee.before') >> (Fig.~\ref{fig:cap}b).

% ======================================================================================== 8 Limitations
\section{Limitations and next steps}\label{sec:limits}
We hold a cheap real option on one number, the stamp lag \(L\), which moves the break-even one for one
(Eq.~\ref{eq:budget}). A live session with a licensed low-latency feed and small test orders measures it, and whether
delayed orders are released on a 1\,s clock (<< V('venue.batch') >> of reprices land just after a whole second); go if
\(L \geq << V('cv.L_go') >>\)\,s. Licensing turns the simulation into deployment (Polymarket itself buys official data;
\citealp{gi2026}); a faster feed moves left on the curve (Fig.~\ref{fig:decay}a). CV accuracy is from table tennis
(illiquid: spread << V('tt.spread') >>¢); tennis is simulated (Fig.~\ref{fig:spin}). Forward test: << V('fwd.cell') >>;
live paper session: << V('live.cell') >>.\label{lastmain}

